  "details": "PlayHapticEventInHand's duration argument does nothing on the steamVR client, it only plays a short vibration for about 0.1 seconds, while the quest and oculus clients play the haptic event as long as expected with the duration argument.\nThis bug is also demonstrated in VRChat's own tutorial on haptic events from 1 and a half year ago: https://youtu.be/95jRByYHE4Y?t=653\nAt 10:53 the vibration only plays very shortly, while in the node at 10:14 the duration says 1 second\nTo reproduce, just use a PlayHapticEventInHand node with any duration and try it on the steamVR client.\nThe headset I'm using is a quest 2 connected via airlink and steamVR if that matters",
